From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] msm: allow P010 scanout on all targets

msm_init() adds BO_USE_SCANOUT and BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER to P010 only
in SC7280 builds. On SC8280XP, 10-bit video in a SurfaceView fails with
"Unsupported combination" (P010 with HW_COMPOSER usage): the decoder
gets no output buffers and reports no error.

Drop the #ifdef. This needs a GPU driver that can sample P010
(patches/mesa/0002): RenderEngine aborts on a P010 buffer it cannot
sample, and on the Huawei MateBook E Go video layers are rotated by the
GPU, so they always reach it.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [needs P010 sampling in the GPU driver, patches/mesa/0002]
---
 msm.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/msm.c b/msm.c
index 90a602c..9fb3472 100644
--- a/msm.c
+++ b/msm.c
@@ -269,10 +269,8 @@ static int msm_init(struct driver *drv)
 	/* Android CTS tests require this. */
 	drv_add_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_BGR888, &LINEAR_METADATA, BO_USE_SW_MASK);
 
-#ifdef SC_7280
 	drv_modify_combination(drv, DRM_FORMAT_P010, &LINEAR_METADATA,
 			       BO_USE_SCANOUT | BO_USE_HW_VIDEO_ENCODER);
-#endif
 
 	drv_modify_linear_combinations(drv);
 
